  "hinge": "The cause is the **choice to treat a law that operates regardless of legislation as though it were a matter of administrative discretion — a standard withdrawn on the finding that it exceeded an agency's authority, a public-health harm dismissed as \"conjectural\", a lock placed against any future administration that might disagree, a war's energy crisis answered by the fuel that was to be phased down, and a mountain range watched at one glacier in two thousand until a town is taken by a failure no instrument recorded.** Verse 191 states the mechanism plainly and without remedy in any court: \"you cannot set yourselves against the creational laws and recommendations without having to bear the consequences in accordance with cause and effect which you determine yourselves through your acting, even if you do not know or refuse to understand this.\" A rescinded rulebook changes what is permitted; it does not change what a warmer atmosphere does. The same law leaves room for a different cause — a standard defended rather than repealed, coal's wartime record answered with capacity and demand rather than with appetite, monitoring funded as infrastructure, removal financed in addition to reduction. Whether the coming decades are remembered as the ones in which a breach was made small and short, or as the ones in which the machinery of self-limitation was dismantled first, is being decided in choices available now — and the effect will follow the cause that is set."
